.venv*/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Agent/tool state. Also covered by some contributors' global gitignore; kept here so a
# fresh clone on any machine is protected without relying on local configuration.
.claude/
.agents/
.superpowers/
.hypothesis/
data/raw/
data/sealed/
data/private/
checkpoints/
adapters/
trackio/
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
access-log.jsonl
# ACL conference style files, fetched locally to typeset the write-ups. NOT vendored: the upstream
# repository (acl-org/acl-style-files) declares NO licence — the GitHub API reports `license: null`
# and there is no LICENSE file — so default copyright applies and we have no redistribution right.
# docs/writeup/acl-template.md records the exact pinned fetch.
docs/writeup/acl-template/
# LaTeX build products. The .tex/.bib are the source; scripts/build_paper.ps1 regenerates the PDF
# in seconds, so the binary is not tracked. docs/writeup/fig/*.pdf IS tracked — that is an input.
docs/writeup/*.aux
docs/writeup/*.bbl
docs/writeup/*.blg
docs/writeup/*.log
docs/writeup/*.out
docs/writeup/*.pdf
!docs/writeup/fig/*.pdf
# The bylined writing-sample variant is DERIVED from the submission .tex by
# `scripts/build_paper.ps1 -Bylined`. Tracking it would create the second copy of the paper the
# generation step exists to avoid.
docs/writeup/*-bylined.tex
# The greyscale proof is a check artefact, regenerated on demand with
# `scripts/plot_risk_coverage.py --greyscale-check`. It is evidence that the figure's
# encoding is redundant, not an input to the paper.
docs/writeup/fig/*-greyscale.png
